  "body": "Hello i'm wondering if a XML SOAP Envelop can be considered a XML without the Prolog part.\r\n\r\n_Maybe it can be a content-type:_  `application/soap+xml`\r\n\r\nThe tested SOAP Envelope was: `<env:Envelope xmlns:env=\"http://www.w3.org/2003/05/soap-envelope\" xmlns:soap=\"http://www.w3.org/2003/05/soap-envelope\"><env:Header><bpeCabecMsg xmlns=\"http://www.portalfiscal.inf.br/bpe\"><cUF xmlns=\"http://www.portalfiscal.inf.br/bpe\">41</cUF><versaoDados xmlns=\"http://www.portalfiscal.inf.br/bpe\">1.00</versaoDados></bpeCabecMsg></env:Header><env:Body xmlns:soap=\"http://www.w3.org/2003/05/soap-envelope\"><bpeStatusServicoBPResult xmlns=\"http://www.portalfiscal.inf.br/bpe/wsdl/BPeStatusServico\"><retConsStatSe`\r\n\r\n**Expected**: `text/xml` or `application/xml` or  `application/soap+xml`\r\n\r\n**Given result**: `text/plain; charset=utf-8`\r\n\r\nProlog meaning: https://www.w3schools.com/xml/xml_syntax.asp\r\n\r\n",
